# villageHall — Mór at the hearth
#
# Mór was originally written in b0.js (the exterior ráth) as a placeholder
# "somewhere reachable" NPC, with her own comment saying she belonged
# inside the hall once the content-loading mechanism existed. That
# mechanism now exists (villageScene.js _loadContent), so she's moved
# here, content otherwise UNCHANGED from the original -- same notes, same
# gating, same voice. Converted from hand-authored JS into .dlg source so
# she's editable through the normal workflow from now on.
#
# Removed from b0.js entirely -- her old exterior "holding position" at
# (30,23) sat close enough to the hall's own door-proximity radius that
# door-proximity (which takes precedence over NPC-proximity every frame)
# would sometimes suppress her badge entirely, so tapping to talk to her
# could walk the player through the door instead. Moving her inside
# removes the collision outright rather than just repositioning her again.
#
# NEW: the final hub gets one additional option, "I think I'll sleep" --
# the settle-by-the-fire beat, completing q_baile and setting has_brat.
# Mór's own ending was previously just a plain goodbye with nothing
# further; this is the only genuinely new content in this file.
#
# NOTES SET HERE (all pre-existing except has_brat)
#   met_mor              -- she exists
#   mor_knows_muireann   -- cross-scene payoff from knows_muireann
#   at_the_fire          -- accepted the seat by the fire
#   knows_seadna_coming  -- told there is a bard in the hall tonight
#   has_brat             -- NEW. mirrors has_toll_rope's pattern: a note
#                           standing in for an item, no inventory system
#   quest q_baile        -- NEW here: q_baile COMPLETES on "I think I'll
#                           sleep" (@done, not @quest -- it was already
#                           started back at Muireann's "Advise me")

@file village/villageHall


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
= node 0 — arrival
@hold
@again Well? / Bhuel?
@note met_mor
Come in out of the rain. You are wet to the skin.
% Tar isteach as an bhfearthainn. Tá tú fliuch go craiceann.

* Muireann sent me
% Muireann a chuir anseo mé
@when note knows_muireann
@note mor_knows_muireann
> Muireann sent me. The woman on the rock at the mouth of the river.
% Muireann a chuir anseo mé. An bhean ar an gcarraig ag béal na habhann.
< Ah. She is still on that rock, so. Sit down.
% Á. Tá sí ar an gcarraig sin fós, mar sin. Suigh síos.

* I am travelling
% Tá mé ag taisteal
@when !note knows_muireann
> I am travelling west. I have never been here before.
% Tá mé ag taisteal siar. Ní raibh mé anseo riamh cheana.
< People do be going west. Sit down.
% Bíonn daoine ag dul siar. Suigh síos.

* Who are you?
% Cé tú féin?
@first
< Mór. This house is mine -- or it is mine when the chieftain is not in it, and he seldom is.
% Mór. Is liomsa an teach seo -- nó is liom é nuair nach mbíonn an taoiseach ann, agus is annamh a bhíonn.

* Farewell
% Slán
@exit
@silent


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
= node 1 — food
There is soup, and bread. Eat.
% Tá anraith ann, agus arán. Ith.

* Thank you
% Go raibh maith agat
> Thank you. I have not had so much as a heel of bread these two days.
% Go raibh maith agat. Ní raibh oiread agus sáil aráin agam le dhá lá.
< Do not mention it. That is how it is here.
% Ná habair é. Sin mar a bhíonn sé anseo.

* What do I owe?
% Cad atá le díol agam?
> What do I owe? I will work for it if needs be.
% Cad atá le díol agam? Oibreoidh mé ar a shon, más gá.
< You will work, is it? In my house? Eat your food.
% Oibreoidh tú, an ea? I dteach s'agamsa? Ith do chuid.

* Not now
% Ní anois
@exit
@silent


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# The teacht drill (nodes 2-4): one verb, four forms, meaning never in
# doubt -- a conjugation drill wearing a joke. USE ONCE, never repeat the
# device elsewhere.

= node 2 — the fire, I
Will you come to the fire?
% An dtiocfaidh tú chun na tine?

* I will come
% Tiocfaidh
> I will come to the fire.
% Tiocfaidh mé chun na tine.

* Not now
% Ní anois
@exit
@silent


= node 3 — the fire, II
Come, then.
% Tar, mar sin.

* I am coming
% Táim ag teacht
> I am coming.
% Táim ag teacht.

* Not now
% Ní anois
@exit
@silent


= node 4 — the fire, III
@note at_the_fire
I see that you are.
% Feicim go bhfuil.

* There is no need to narrate it
% Ní gá é a insint
< Ha! Sit down, stranger, and be quiet.
% Ha! Suigh síos, a stróinséir, agus bí i do thost.

* Not now
% Ní anois
@exit
@silent


# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
= node 5 — the hub
@hold
@again Well? / Bhuel?
You have the fire, and your belly is full. Do not be stirring.
% Tá an tine agat, agus do bholg lán. Ná bí ag corraí.

* Is there news?
% An bhfuil scéal ann?
@first
@note knows_seadna_coming
> Is there any news in this house?
% An bhfuil scéal ar bith sa teach seo?
< We have a poet these three weeks. He will be singing tonight. Wait until you hear him.
% Tá file againn le trí seachtaine. Beidh sé ag gabháil fhoinn anocht. Fan go gcloisfidh tú é.

* Who is the chieftain?
% Cé hé an taoiseach?
@first
> Who is the chieftain here? Whose land is this?
% Cé hé an taoiseach anseo? Cé leis an talamh seo?
< Fionnbarra. He is in the hall more now than he used to be.
% Fionnbarra. Bíonn sé sa halla níos mó anois ná mar a bhíodh.

* I saw a man on the road
% Chonaic mé fear ar an mbóthar
@when note met_briugu
@first
> I saw a man on the road, going east. He would not say why.
% Chonaic mé fear ar an mbóthar, agus é ag imeacht soir. Ní déarfadh sé cad chuige.
< ...  He had a house. Eat your food now.
% ...  Bhí teach aige. Ith do chuid anois.

* I think I'll sleep
% Sílim go luífidh mé
@note has_brat
@done q_baile
> I have had enough of tonight, I think. I'll sleep, if I may.
% Sílim go bhfuil mo dhóthain agam den oíche seo. Luífidh mé, más é do thoil é.
< Seven days you've been on that river, by the look of you.
% Seacht lá atá caite agat ar an abhainn sin, de réir do chuma.
< Rest the limbs. You are not where you meant to be, but you are safe.
% Lig do do ghéaga. Níl tú san áit a raibh tú ag dul, ach tá tú slán.
< The fire is warm, and the pot smells better than it looks.
% Tá an tine te, agus tá boladh níos fearr ón bpota ná mar a fheictear air.
< Someone drapes a heavy brat over your shoulders as your eyes close.
% Sínítear brat trom thar do ghuaillí agus do shúile ag dúnadh.

* Goodbye for now
% Slán go fóill
@exit
@silent
